s thick fur and sleeps in trees.'' Whether those claims are true depends on the animal and must be verified. Useful feedback uses the original evidence or language point.","options":["''The animal has thick fur and sleeps in trees.'' Whether those claims are true depends on the animal and must be verified.","A spellchecker cannot establish that a factual claim is accurate or that a caption matches a diagram.","Any answer is equally supported.","There is no need to compare your attempt."],"question":"After trying \"Correct the language in ''The animal have thick fur and it sleep in trees''; ident\", which feedback is most useful?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"The most useful evidence is a specific choice in the example, followed by an explanation of the effect on meaning. Useful feedback uses the original evidence or language point.","options":["The most useful evidence is a specific choice in the example, followed by an explanation of the effect on meaning.","Saying a choice is good without naming the actual detail does not show understanding.","Any answer is equally supported.","There is no need to compare your attempt."],"question":"After trying \"Underline or quote one precise detail in the model and explain its effect.\", which feedback is most useful?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"''The animal has thick fur and sleeps in trees.'' Whether those claims are true depends on the animal and must be verified. Useful feedback uses the original evidence or language point.","options":["''The animal has thick fur and sleeps in trees.'' Whether those claims are true depends on the animal and must be verified.","A superficial change in length or appearance does not repair meaning. A spellchecker cannot establish that a factual claim is accurate or that a caption matches a diagram.","Any answer is equally supported.","There is no need to compare your attempt."],"question":"After trying \"Describe why the warned-against approach would weaken your work, then write a co\", which feedback is most useful?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"The new example should meet the same purpose as the model, but contain original material. Useful feedback uses the original evidence or language point.","options":["The new example should meet the same purpose as the model, but contain original material.","Repeating the worked example cannot show transfer to new content.","Any answer is equally supported.","There is no need to compare your attempt."],"question":"After trying \"Make one fresh example demonstrating the skill and explain your main choice.\", which feedback is most useful?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"explanation":"Independent evidence, not repetition of the worked model, demonstrates the skill.","marking_guide":"Require independently produced relevant work with accurate reasoning and a specific supporting detail.","question":"Produce a fresh example demonstrating the central skill, explaining the particular words or evidence that make it work.","sample_answer":"Original demonstration: Draft: ''Koalas eats leaves. They live all over the world.'' Revision: ''Koalas eat mainly eucalypt leaves. They occur naturally in parts of eastern Australia.'' I would verify range and diet with an authoritative source before publishing.","type":"short_answer"},{"explanation":"A correction needs to change meaning or accuracy, not just make the text longer.","marking_guide":"Require an actual misconception plus corrected example and purpose-linked explanation.","question":"Name one likely error in using this skill, correct it and explain why the correction helps.","sample_answer":"Common error: A spellchecker cannot establish that a factual claim is accurate or that a caption matches a diagram. Correction: ''The animal has thick fur and sleeps in trees.'' Whether those claims are true depends on the animal and must be verified.","type":"short_answer"}],"resources":null,"res